.TH ATTACK-SURFACE 1 "2026" "attack-surface 0.17" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
attack\-surface \- modular attack\-surface reconnaissance and monitoring toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B attack\-surface.py
\fB\-d\fR \fIdomain\fR [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B attack\-surface
discovers and grades the external attack surface of a domain:
subdomain discovery, host liveness, service/port banners (nmap \-sV),
security\-header auditing, technology fingerprinting, CDN/origin
detection, admin\-panel discovery, exposed CMS setup pages,
subdomain\-takeover fingerprints, baseline diffing for continuous
monitoring, CPE\-exact CVE watchlists (NVD), safe active checks
(TLS audit, login liveness, DNS AXFR/DNSSEC) and SOC telemetry
(CEF syslog, Slack, Telegram).
.PP
All discovery is scope\-checked and rate\-limited. Results are exported
as HTML (XSS\-safe), CSV, Markdown, JSON and NDJSON streams.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIdomain\fR
Primary target domain (required).
.TP
.BR \-\-rate " " \fIn\fR
Max requests per second (token bucket, default 5).
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-ports
Skip the nmap phase entirely.
.TP
.BR \-\-scope " " \fIfile\fR
Enforce target scope from file (one host per line; warn|soft|strict).
.TP
.BR \-\-cves
Keyword CVE watchlist from NVD (fast, some noise).
.TP
.BR \-\-cves\-deep
Exact CPE\-matching CVE scan (NVD CPE API). Preferred.
.TP
.BR \-\-poc
Safe active probes: TLS audit/grade, login liveness (one attempt),
DNS AXFR + DNSSEC check. Never destructive.
.TP
.BR \-\-syslog " " \fIhost[:port]\fR
Stream CEF events to a SIEM collector over UDP syslog.
.TP
.BR \-\-webhook " " \fIurl\fR
Push high/critical alerts to a Slack\-compatible webhook.
.TP
.BR \-\-tg\-token " " \fItoken\fR
Telegram bot token for on\-call alerts (with \fB\-\-tg\-chat\fR).
.TP
.BR \-\-tg\-chat " " \fIchat_id\fR
Telegram chat id for on\-call alerts.
.TP
.BR \-\-resume " " \fIfile\fR
Resume an interrupted scan from its checkpoint.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-baseline
Disable blue\-team baseline diffing for this run.
.TP
.BR \-\-update
Self\-update from the configured Git remote.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I reports/
All generated artifacts (html/, baselines/, output.json, ...).
.TP
.I wordlists/
Bundled wordlists (common subdomain prefixes, panel paths).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success. Non\-zero on configuration or fatal errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Full scan with versioned banners and safe PoC:
.B attack\-surface.py \-d example.com \-\-cves\-deep \-\-poc
.TP
Daily monitoring with Telegram alerts:
.B attack\-surface.py \-d example.com \-\-no\-ports \-\-tg\-token BOT \-\-tg\-chat CHAT
.SH LEGAL
Only scan systems you own or have explicit written permission to test.
The scope module exists to enforce that. Misuse is your responsibility.
